{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/631720-build-help","id":631720,"title":"Build Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-18T16:47:00-07:00","id":631720,"title":"Build Help","content":"Hey. I am reading the 2nd edition of Werewolf: The Forsaken but I am not as well versed in the game as some. I know a number of you are much more knowledgeable about it then I am. I am looking for help to make an ass kicking beginners build. A bookworm who just experienced his first change. He would be at starting level. I am open to whatever you guys might like to make? I figured if I have an experienced build make my starting character I can build off that and start game play. Or its gonna take me weeks before I can do that reading thru this book. Any help is greatly appreciated. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4505-hairhero","name":"HairHero","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T17:12:37-07:00","id":631751,"title":"","content":"Well, what do you want your character to do and be? If you describe your character's personality and your goals as a player it'll be a lot easier. Builds aren't really so much a thing in NWoD, since the sheet tends to follow the character and not the other way around.<br /> <br /> Going by what you've described all I can really say is that you'll want decent Intelligence and Academics scores. And the Library merit and the Sift the Sands Knowledge facet couldn't hurt. Anything more and I'd just be making a random character for you.<br /> <br /> The Bone Shadows and Iron Masters would both make good tribes for what you've described, though you could go another direction entirely. Similarly Ithaeur would make a good fit as far as Auspice, but again, even that is flexible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 08-18-2015, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T17:53:09-07:00","id":631777,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Harisson has a complex personality that many never explore in its entirety. He is daunting and possessed of many layers. On the surface, many see gentle kindness and a soft-spoken, delicate young man. Certainly concern for others is something that shows through in his relations with them. He rarely raises his voice in conversation, unless it is necessary or unless something has deeply affected him. Similarly, he tries not to be unnecessarily confrontational, considering that it might be hurtful.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\">He is not deceptive, but he is not an open book, by any means. To most, he shows a disciplined, deeply focused individual, able to withstand whatever could be thrown at him. Even if others cannot be strong, his unique position forces him to do so. If allowed to become more familiar with him, his friends will find a perhaps surprisingly vulnerable man, one who must maintain his strength so that he of all people will believe in it. He would like to be cared for, but more important on his list of priorities is the protection of others, the caring for others so that they will be able to live fully.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Nonetheless, he is remarkably sensitive and can sympathise with others effortlessly. He knows when the time is right to show what is necessary, in order to win the trust of another or to show them that he is acting in good faith, or that they may reciprocate. He is very sensitive to the things that others will respond to, naturally, and tends to employ this empathy in his relations with others. Yet he carefully makes it so that most will not get too close to him, for their safety and his own. He often maintains himself as an outsider until or unless he can be persuaded otherwise.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\">It can be difficult to get him to volunteer information unless it is directly applicable to the situation at hand. Usually he is not a fan of filling a void with chatter, but he can discuss intelligent topics in depth. Meaningless chit-chat does not fit into his area of expertise, and it may contribute to others thinking that he might be awkward in certain situations. He can and does express himself freely, though, and that occurs not only through words, but through actions. When he meets someone to whom he can relate deeply or easily, he will express himself in his unique ways to them; to him, communication occurs on so many levels, and only one of those happens to be the verbal level.<br /> <br /> He loves to read. He has an interest in the occult since his change. I could go Shaman/Spirits but what my current weakness is making a +sheet that works best with stats, merits, skills, and gifts.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4505-hairhero","user":"HairHero","date":". 08-18-2015, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4505-hairhero","name":"HairHero","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T20:25:11-07:00","id":631846,"title":"","content":"First, you won't be shaman. You'll be an Elodoth, social thinker, strategist, diplomat and judge. It is perfect for you.<br /> <br /> Attributes, Mental &gt; Social &gt; Physical, emphasizes Composure, Resolve, Intelligence and Manipulation.<br /> <br /> Skills you'll probably go the other way around, making Social the higher category. Empathy is the obvious fit, but add Persuasion and Subterfuge, at least, and maybe Expression and Socialize. Then go for Mental and distribute as you see fit, just remember to add something to Occult. Your concept accepts whatever you do at the Physical skills, but if you want mechanical advice, you can put Athletics high without shame if you don't have uses for the others. You won't have a very combative role, so it will just bump your Defense.<br /> <br /> Your description calls easily for Storm Lord as tribe, very fitting, and gives you a second Honor point.For Merits go to General Werewolf Merits section. Anchored, Code of Honor and Controlled Burn can take your attention, but are probably better to take later. Take Impartial Mediator, Moon-Kissed, Residential Area 4 and Strings of the Heart immediately. Those will give you the tools to work with people with extreme ease, though Impartial Mediator can be ditched for other Mental or Social Human Merits of your liking, and even to raise Residential Area to 5.<br /> <br /> Take your third dot of Renown on Cunning and go for Gifts, you'll start with the two Half-Moon's Gifts of lower levels anyway. One to discern lies, other to seal oaths and pacts. Good for ya. In the Gift of Dominance, take Primal Allure, the Cunning Facet, that will make you a veritable social shark in shallow waters, able to make a stranger lend you his own daughter for the night if you wish. The Gift of Insight give you Prey on Weakness as the Cunning Facet, that enables you to gather precious information about people and use those to become even more convincing. Starting rites is a thing to be discussed with your group, as is the possibility of taking some of the Merit points for the Totem.<br /> <br /> Here you have. You can fill the few gaps. Most relevant, yet, you can read the book yourself during the time you have and tweak whatever you want. This build is just a narrow focused approach over the idea of your character being defined by how he relates to people. It is a bit overkill in that regard, but guarantees effectiveness, and is relatively simple to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 08-19-2015, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T04:13:38-07:00","id":632142,"title":"","content":"Perseverance? Does that stand for Resolve or Presence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T11:06:12-07:00","id":632535,"title":"","content":"Resolve, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> 